<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbek May gas output falls to 4.1 bcm vs 4.3 in Ap.</title>
<headline>Uzbek May gas output falls to 4.1 bcm vs 4.3 in Ap.</headline>
<dateline>TASHKENT 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbekistan's production of natural gas fell in May to 4.1 billion cubic meters from 4.3 billion cubic meters in April, the State Statistics Committee said on Friday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical bulletin. (Figures in tonnes, except natural gas in billion cubic meters and crude oil in million tonnes).</p>
<p>    UZBEK ENERGY OUTPUT	MAY 97   APR 97  JAN-MAY 97</p>
<p>    Natural gas		     4.1	4.3	  21.9</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change	     +2.7     +0.7	  +0.6</p>
<p>    Crude oil			 0.7	0.7	   3.3</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change	     +5,8     -4.4	  +4.3</p>
<p>    Gasoline			 92,300  113,000     548,600</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change	    -17.3     +1.8	  +1.7</p>
<p>    Diesel			  177,300  176,200     824,500</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change	    +12.9     +9.7	  +7.7</p>
<p>    Fuel oil			175,500  176,700     883,000</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change	     -1.3    +12.0	  -9.7</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
